    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a constrained offensive outlook, as the majority of our core, including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**, are off the field due to league scheduling. With the roster depth thinned, we are leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** to anchor the lineup against Misiorowski. **Kyle Tucker** presents the strongest play with an efficiency score of 47.99, though the projection is significantly suppressed by Misiorowski\u2019s elite 2.35 xERA. While **Kyle Tucker** retains high recency value, his drop to the #8 hole in the order\u2014a decision likely influenced by team-specific adjustments\u2014minimizes his counting stat potential. **Andy Pages** occupies the UTIL spot with a score of 42.38, showing marginal utility; his lack of a platoon edge against the right-handed Misiorowski, combined with an unfavorable batting order position, keeps his ceiling firmly capped in the low 40s.\n\nRegarding our bench composition, the decision to leave our remaining depth assets sidelined is straightforward, as the lack of games for **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** leaves no viable alternatives. The most significant concern remains the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to occupy a roster spot while on the IL, providing zero value to our 5x5 Roto effort. We must remain cautious of the matchup against Misiorowski; his sub-3.00 xERA is a primary factor in the depressed scoring across the board, and any slight deviation in command from the pitcher will be necessary for **Kyle Tucker** or **Andy Pages** to outperform their current marginal projections.",
